  "details": "I really liked the way the 2.0 avatars did the auto footsteps when crouched, it looked very natural like you are squatting down. In 3.0 avatars you can do many more things, but every single animation just looks \"fake\" because there is no psuedo-natural movement. On top of that, comparing the default crouching animations of sdk 2 and 3, I think it would make a really good default animation to combine the two of them (also, I am talking about the prone animations). The way I am thinking is by adding the way the arms are in the sdk 3 default and the leg squat from sdk 2. Also, I know having this on by default could mess up some custom animations, so there could be an option like how there is for 6-point tracking and 3 and 4-point tracking. Also, I'm going to add some screenshots for reference, 2 of sdk 3 crouch when rotating from side to side and also 2 from sdk 2 doing the same thing. This is for clarity and to note the change in position of the feet when idle and rotating. I just wanna do happy squats :3 Thanks!",
